{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/2339","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/2339/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/2339/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/2339/events","html_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/issues/2339","id":46928467,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NjkyODQ2Nw==","number":2339,"title":"Chain as chord body on redis broken (when new_join=1)","user":{"login":"cheif","id":678919,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODkxOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif","html_url":"https://github.com/cheif","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheif/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":46814,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0NjgxNA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/labels/Status:%20Confirmed%20%E2%9C%94","name":"Status: Confirmed ✔","color":"ff9900","default":false,"description":null},{"id":81929225,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4MTkyOTIyNQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/labels/Component:%20Redis%20Broker","name":"Component: Redis Broker","color":"4c3491","default":false,"description":null},{"id":235024002,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzUwMjQwMDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/labels/Issue%20Type:%20Bug%20Report","name":"Issue Type: Bug Report","color":"e11d21","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2014-10-27T16:41:15Z","updated_at":"2015-07-18T06:53:16Z","closed_at":"2014-10-29T17:29:17Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi, I'm using celery with a redis-backend and just tried to create a chord which had a chain as a callback, but it seems like this implementation is broken.\n\n```\n@task\ndef ret_one():\n    return 1\n\n@task\ndef chain1(res):\n    return res*2\n\n@task\ndef chain2(res):\n    return res+2\n\ntasks = [ret_one.s() for _ in range(10)]\nbody = chain1 | chain2\n\nchord(tasks, body).delay()\n```\n\nIn this case the chord-call seems to fail, since the redis handler for result tries to get 'chord_size' from the signature of the chain, which raises KeyError. https://github.com/celery/celery/blob/master/celery/backends/redis.py#L222\n\nA simpler example:\n\n```\nfrom celery.canvas import maybe_signature\nd = {'subtask_type': 'chain', 'kwargs': {'tasks': ()}, 'options': {}, 'chord_size': 11}\ns = maybe_signature(d)\ns['chord_size'] <== raises KeyError\n```\n\nThis seems to work when subtask_type isn't set, i.e. the callback is a normal task. But raises on all different types of tasks.\n\nI'm not really sure if this is a bug, or if I'm doing something wrong, but it seems like the other backends don't look for callback['chord_size'] atleast, and the documentation doesn't mention that you can't use chains as the body for a chord.\n","closed_by":{"login":"ask","id":1558,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1558?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ask"